{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"foil method foil method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md","fileName":"FOIL Method.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"FOIL Method","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial and Rational Expressions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Binomial","Distributive Property","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"foil method foil method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md","fileName":"FOIL Method.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"FOIL Method","heading":"FOIL Method","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The FOIL method is a mnemonic for multiplying two [[Binomial]]s. It names the First, Outside, Inside, and Last term products so that every term of one factor is multiplied by every term of the other.\n\nFor ((a+b)(c+d)), the four products are (ac), (ad), (bc), and (bd). Their sum is then simplified by combining like terms. FOIL is not a separate algebraic law and does not generalize by its name to polynomials with more terms; the underlying rule is the [[Distributive Property]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Binomial","Distributive Property","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"foil method foil method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/FOIL Method.md","fileName":"FOIL Method.md","folder":"6